      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STARBURST (5) is a lightly raced mare who switched to this track last start and just found a handy horse too strong. This doesn't look any harder and she should find the front fairly comfortably for Olivia East who can rate a leader. Expect she gives a huge sight. BLISS BOMB (2) was well below her best last time in tougher company. That was on heavy ground which clearly didn't suit. Back onto synthetic should suit nicely and she should bounce back. HUSTLE (4) resumes having gone to the paddock a winner at Kyneton in this grade. First go on synthetic but draws well and has claims. FAST 'N' INZAINE (3) ran a solid race first up here in a BM62 and should be fitter. She's got upside and should take holding out. BRAVE CAROL (1) is a minor hope.",
